{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":14577270,"name":"Junyuyuan","username":"Junyuyuan","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/devforum.roblox.com/junyuyuan/{size}/8664759_2.png","created_at":"2026-07-10T10:08:34.249Z","cooked":"\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-14577270-bug-description-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-14577270-bug-description-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eBug Description\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhen Roblox Studio is opened \u003cstrong\u003eafter\u003c/strong\u003e \u003ccode\u003eStudioMCP.exe\u003c/code\u003e is already running, \u003ccode\u003elist_roblox_studios\u003c/code\u003e returns an empty list (with the note “The previously active Studio instance has disconnected”), even though the Studio instance is running and the MCP panel inside Studio shows “connected”.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe MCP panel UI inside Studio displays a connected state, but the StudioMCP server-side session is stale and cannot discover the newly opened Studio window.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-14577270-reproduction-steps-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-14577270-reproduction-steps-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eReproduction Steps\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eHave at least one Studio window open → MCP is working normally\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eClose that Studio window (StudioMCP may continue running as a background process)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOpen a \u003cstrong\u003enew\u003c/strong\u003e Studio window (a different place/project)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eCall \u003ccode\u003elist_roblox_studios\u003c/code\u003e via MCP client\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eExpected:\u003c/strong\u003e The new Studio instance appears in the list\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eActual:\u003c/strong\u003e Returns empty list with \u003ccode\u003e\"previously active Studio instance has disconnected\"\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-14577270-root-cause-investigated-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-14577270-root-cause-investigated-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eRoot Cause (investigated)\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThrough process and network analysis, the issue was traced to:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ccode\u003eStudioMCP.exe\u003c/code\u003e communicates with \u003ccode\u003eRobloxStudioBeta.exe\u003c/code\u003e via a \u003cstrong\u003enamed pipe\u003c/strong\u003e named \u003ccode\u003eRBX_STUDIO_NS-{PID}\u003c/code\u003e, where \u003ccode\u003e{PID}\u003c/code\u003e is the Studio process ID.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eWhen Studio closes, the pipe is destroyed.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eWhen a \u003cstrong\u003enew\u003c/strong\u003e Studio window opens (with a new PID), it creates a new pipe \u003ccode\u003eRBX_STUDIO_NS-{newPID}\u003c/code\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eHowever, the already-running \u003ccode\u003eStudioMCP.exe\u003c/code\u003e process does \u003cstrong\u003enot\u003c/strong\u003e automatically discover the new pipe. It retains stale state from the previous session.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAs a result, the MCP \u003ccode\u003einitialize\u003c/code\u003e handshake fails (\u003ccode\u003econnection closed: initialize request\u003c/code\u003e), and no Studio instances are returned.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWorkaround:\u003c/strong\u003e Manually opening the MCP panel widget inside Studio forces the plugin to re-register with \u003ccode\u003eStudioMCP\u003c/code\u003e, which unblocks subsequent calls. However, this is not intuitive and requires user intervention every time Studio is reopened.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-14577270-expected-behavior-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-14577270-expected-behavior-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eExpected Behavior\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ccode\u003eStudioMCP\u003c/code\u003e should either:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAutomatically scan for active \u003ccode\u003eRBX_STUDIO_NS-*\u003c/code\u003e named pipes on each \u003ccode\u003elist_roblox_studios\u003c/code\u003e call, or\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eImplement a reconnection/discovery mechanism when a new Studio window is detected\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-14577270-environment-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-14577270-environment-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eEnvironment\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eRoblox Studio Version: \u003ccode\u003e0.729.0.7290838\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eStudioMCP Version: \u003ccode\u003eversion-4bb3958a2cde4efb\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOS: Windows 11\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eReproduced consistently when: closing one Studio window and opening a new one while StudioMCP remains in memory\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-14577270-additional-notes-6\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-14577270-additional-notes-6\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eAdditional Notes\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePreviously (with a single Studio window workflow), this issue does not occur because StudioMCP restarts together with Studio. The bug surfaces specifically in multi-window or sequential-open workflows.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":4,"updated_at":"2026-07-10T10:08:34.249Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":257,"reads":77,"readers_count":76,"score":1360.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":4729586,"topic_slug":"studiomcp-fails-to-list-studio-instances-after-new-studio-window-opens-while-studiomcp-is-already-running","display_username":"Junyuyuan","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"Programmer","title_is_group":false,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":4}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":465129,"hidden":false,"trust_level":1,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/studiomcp-fails-to-list-studio-instances-after-new-studio-window-opens-while-studiomcp-is-already-running/4729586/1","can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_translate":false,"is_translated":false,"detected_language":"English"},{"id":14579852,"name":"Sonebuilder","username":"SoneBuiIder","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/devforum.roblox.com/sonebuiider/{size}/8939587_2.png","created_at":"2026-07-11T00:03:14.665Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eAnd it burns so much usage trying to find other bridges \u003cimg src=\"https://doy2mn9upadnk.cloudfront.net/images/emoji/twitter/face_holding_back_tears.png?v=14\" title=\":face_holding_back_tears:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":face_holding_back_tears:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":2,"post_type":1,"posts_count":4,"updated_at":"2026-07-11T00:03:14.665Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":2,"reads":52,"readers_count":51,"score":20.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":4729586,"topic_slug":"studiomcp-fails-to-list-studio-instances-after-new-studio-window-opens-while-studiomcp-is-already-running","display_username":"Sonebuilder","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"Programmer","title_is_group":false,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,